17592186394738 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}11 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 9\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{74}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394739 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394740 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394739 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394739 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394739 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394743 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394739 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/r